title: lirael_first_appearance
---
Lirael: *(translucent, humming a melody you can almost place)*
Lirael: Why do grown-ups build houses then live in the attic?
Lirael: Hello. I don't remember my name. Only the song.
===

title: lirael_lullaby
---
Lirael: My mother sang me a lullaby on the train.
Lirael: *(she hums — 432 Hz, then descending fourths)*
Lirael: I sang to keep the mud away. But the song broke. And then I was here. And then I forgot.
===

title: lirael_calendar_echo
---
Lirael: They put us on a calendar — thirteen months, twenty-eight days each, and one day out of time.
Lirael: Day Out of Time. That's where I went when the song broke.
Lirael: Day Twenty-Five. That's the day. Will you remember?
===

title: lirael_explains_prophecy
---
Lirael: The skeleton in the hand has a voice. It hums prophecies.
Lirael: Stand near it during the seventeenth hour. The light will speak.
Lirael: I don't know what it will say. But I will be afraid for you.
===

title: lirael_farewell
---
Lirael: Goodbye for now, traveler.
Lirael: *(she fades — but the humming continues, embedded in the dome's acoustic)*
Lirael: When you sing, sing for me.
===
